# 5. Phase 1 — Development Environment

## Goal

Prepare the laptop for application development.

Planned tools:

- VS Code
- Git
- GitHub
- Flutter SDK
- Dart
- Python
- FastAPI
- PostgreSQL
- Postman or equivalent API testing tool
- Terminal / PowerShell

## Learning

Understand:

- What an application is
- What frontend means
- What backend means
- What a database does
- How applications communicate
- How to run applications locally

---

# 6. Phase 2 — Git

## Goal

Learn version control.

Git allows us to track changes to the project.

Example:

```text
Version 1
   ↓
Change code
   ↓
Version 2
   ↓
Something breaks
   ↓
Compare previous version
```

## Topics

Learn:

- git init
- git status
- git add
- git commit
- git log
- git diff
- git branch
- git checkout / switch
- git merge
- git pull
- git push
- .gitignore

## Project Usage

Every meaningful project change should be committed.

Example:

```text
feat: add expense API
fix: correct expense validation
docs: update database design
```

---

# 7. Phase 3 — GitHub

## Goal

Use GitHub as the central source-code repository.

Repository:

```text
my-life-os
```

GitHub will contain:

- Source code
- Documentation
- Configuration templates
- Tests
- CI/CD workflows
- Infrastructure code

It must NOT contain:

- Passwords
- API keys
- Database credentials
- AWS credentials
- Personal financial records
- Private spreadsheet data
- Other sensitive information

---

