# 16. Phase 10 — Terraform

## Goal

Learn Infrastructure as Code.

Instead of manually creating infrastructure:

```text
Click AWS Console
Click settings
Create resource
Configure resource
```

Terraform allows infrastructure to be described as code.

Concept:

```text
Terraform Code
      ↓
Terraform
      ↓
AWS Infrastructure
```

Topics:

- Providers
- Resources
- Variables
- Outputs
- State
- Modules
- Plan
- Apply
- Destroy

Terraform must never contain hardcoded secrets.

---

# 17. Phase 11 — Kubernetes

## Goal

Learn container orchestration.

Kubernetes will NOT be introduced at the beginning.

First learn:

```text
Application
↓
Docker
↓
Docker Compose
↓
Cloud
```

Then Kubernetes.

Learning progression:

```text
Kind / Minikube
      ↓
Pods
      ↓
Deployments
      ↓
Services
      ↓
ConfigMaps
      ↓
Secrets
      ↓
Ingress
      ↓
Health Checks
      ↓
AWS EKS
```

---

# 18. Kubernetes Learning Principle

Kubernetes should solve a real problem.

Do not move the application to Kubernetes simply because Kubernetes is on the DevOps roadmap.

First understand:

- Why containers are needed
- Why multiple containers exist
- Why orchestration is useful
- What happens when a container fails
- How traffic reaches an application
- How configuration is managed

